% SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2
% =====================================================================
% queries.clausal -- QUERY-COMBINATOR layer for eu/ai_act/small_items.
% A TOP-LAYER consumer: it imports the determination slice's PUBLIC
% predicates it calls, and nothing else.
%
% Source: Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 (Artificial Intelligence Act), consolidated
% text 02024R1689-20260727 (as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744). This layer
% decides no statutory condition: every answer comes from the slice.
%
% Query types served (all through the slice small_items.clausal):
%   #3  status_determination: the six queries and small_items_status/2
%       (re-exported by the package facade);
%   #13 compliance_check: is the proposed processing, testing or reliance
%       allowed: decide_small_items/2, whose verdict carries the RESULT atom of
%       the matching query (for example real_world_testing_permitted or
%       real_world_testing_not_permitted) with its citations;
%   #7  justification: small_items_checklist/2 in the slice, one
%       item(Requirement, Status, cite(Key)) per condition;
%   #16 what-if: small_items_what_if/4 below.
%
% small_items_what_if(Request, Key, Value, Status): Request is the facade term
%   small_items_request(Query, Profile, AssessmentDate); attribute(Key, Value)
%   replaces every attribute of Key in the attribute-list Profile (or is added
%   when Key is absent) and the query is asked again. The kit override_key/4
%   works on dicts, and this order types the profile as an attribute list, so
%   the replacement is local list plumbing (noted for the kit in the working notes (not published)).
% small_items_profile_keys/1: the sixty-three profile keys, contract order.
% small_items_input_problems/2: THE INPUT CHECK, re-exported from the kernel.
%
% ROOT EXPORTS (the order's export requirement): the sixty-three profile key
% atoms, the seventeen enumeration atoms, the judgement value unsure and the
% result atoms of the six queries are served here as facts, so the package
% root exposes each of them by name. The result constructors are served as
% guarded well-formedness checks: each holds exactly for a term of the shape
% the called contract gives it. They decide nothing: they are the vocabulary
% of the called contract.
% =====================================================================

